-- RecallFence: the audit sink (graft 2).
--
-- Template. apply.sh substitutes @@SINK_URI@@, built from RF_S3_BUCKET,
-- RF_S3_PREFIX and the scoped IAM key fetched from Secrets Manager. The rendered
-- SQL is never written to disk, because the URI carries a live secret access key.
--
-- Spike 4, on the live cluster:
--
--   * Changefeeds into an external sink work on the Basic tier. No enterprise
--     upgrade needed for this build.
--   * Implicit credentials are refused outright:
--       ERROR: implicit credentials disallowed for s3 due to
--              --external-io-disable-implicit-credentials flag
--     There is no instance-profile path on Cloud. The key goes in the URI, which
--     is exactly why it comes from Secrets Manager and never from the repo.
--   * Delivery is in seconds, as NDJSON, one object per resolved window.
--   * The changefeed principal can be denied s3:DeleteObject and still work, so
--     the sink is append-only to the writer as well as to everyone else.
--   * An idle changefeed still writes RESOLVED markers every 10s, so silence in
--     the bucket means the feed died rather than nothing having happened.
--
-- The bucket is not what makes the record tamper-evident. The hash chain is:
-- receipts.receipt_hash digests the body plus prev_receipt_hash, so altering any
-- earlier receipt breaks every later one, and that property survives an attacker
-- with write access to S3. Spike 4 verified a three-receipt chain against the
-- delivered object.

-- No `SET CLUSTER SETTING kv.rangefeed.enabled` here.
--
-- On CockroachDB Cloud that setting is operator-managed and already on, and
-- attempting it fails with "setting kv.rangefeed.enabled is only settable by the
-- operator" (42501). Because statements are piped in as one batch, that error
-- aborted the batch and the changefeed was never created. It is a self-hosted
-- step that does not apply here.

CREATE CHANGEFEED FOR TABLE receipts
  INTO '@@SINK_URI@@'
  WITH
    format = json,
    envelope = wrapped,
    updated,
    resolved = '10s',
    min_checkpoint_frequency = '10s';
